        "original_id": "3f0b0873-6182-5331-8eb5-b344ea780d10",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Gambon, Albus Dumbledore, Richard Harris, Michael Lombard, Bates, Lord Voldemort\n- Organizations: BBC, ITV, Order of the Phoenix\n- Works: The Singing Detective, Maigret, Harry Potter, Otherwise Engaged\n- Roles: mystery writer protagonist, Jules Maigret, Professor Albus Dumbledore\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Michael Gambon took over from Bates in Otherwise Engaged and played the role for a year, eight times a week.\n- In 1977, Michael Lombard was nominated for a Drama Desk Award for his performance in Otherwise Engaged.\n- Michael Gambon played the eponymous mystery writer protagonist in the BBC television serial The Singing Detective.\n- Michael Gambon played Jules Maigret in the 1990s ITV serial Maigret.\n- After Richard Harris died, Michael Gambon played Professor Albus Dumbledore in the final six Harry Potter films.\n- Albus Dumbledore is the founder and leader of the Order of the Phoenix, an organisation dedicated to fighting Lord Voldemort.",
